            <ArticleTitle>True aneurysms of the superficial temporal artery: report of three cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>687.e15-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.avsg.2009.03.011</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Superficial temporal artery aneurysms account for &lt;1% of reported aneurysms. The majority of these aneurysms are a consequence of trauma; however, true superficial temporal artery aneurysms are extremely rare. Here, we present three cases of spontaneous superficial temporal artery aneurysms arising without any previous history of trauma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
